WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.644 --> 00:00:02.395
- [Voiceover] Why are some couples happy,

00:00:02.395 --> 00:00:04.409
and some are straight up miserable?

00:00:04.409 --> 00:00:05.960
- I will stop acting like your mom

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.751
when you stop acting like a child.

00:00:07.751 --> 00:00:09.537
- What, are you on your period?

00:00:09.537 --> 00:00:12.120
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.841 --> 00:00:16.059
(symphony music)

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:17.919
- One way to understand
how relationships work

00:00:17.919 --> 00:00:21.215
is the concept of Attachment Theory.

00:00:21.215 --> 00:00:22.945
Attachment Theory is the idea

00:00:22.945 --> 00:00:25.467
that the way that your
parents treated you as a baby

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:28.505
affects you in your romantic
relationships as an adult.

00:00:28.505 --> 00:00:29.506
(crunch)

00:00:29.506 --> 00:00:31.119
Mmm. Apple-y.

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:31.952
(smack)

00:00:31.952 --> 00:00:33.882
There are three types of adult attachment:

00:00:33.882 --> 00:00:36.382
secure, anxious, and avoidant.

00:00:38.201 --> 00:00:40.862
- A securely attached person
has healthy relationships.

00:00:40.862 --> 00:00:42.176
They are confident that
their needs will be met

00:00:42.176 --> 00:00:44.530
by their partner and
they can depend on them.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.164
- All right, I attempted
to make a latte for you.

00:00:47.164 --> 00:00:49.735
- Aww thank you. I saved
you the calendar section.

00:00:49.735 --> 00:00:50.796
- Where's my latte?

00:00:50.796 --> 00:00:52.397
- Who are you?

00:00:52.397 --> 00:00:54.332
- How'd you get in our house?

00:00:54.332 --> 00:00:55.165
(whoosh)

00:00:55.165 --> 00:00:58.237
- An anxious person has a fear
of rejection and abandonment,

00:00:58.237 --> 00:00:59.638
so they're always worried

00:00:59.638 --> 00:01:02.945
that their partner will leave them.

00:01:02.945 --> 00:01:04.429
- So where are you going?

00:01:04.429 --> 00:01:05.549
Are you mad at me?

00:01:05.549 --> 00:01:06.758
- I'm going to the bathroom.

00:01:06.758 --> 00:01:08.675
- Oh, okay, I love you.

00:01:09.984 --> 00:01:11.254
Uh, don't you wanna say someth-

00:01:11.254 --> 00:01:12.987
- Uh, I love you too.

00:01:12.987 --> 00:01:15.016
- Thank you. Text me.

00:01:15.016 --> 00:01:16.919
- A person with an
avoidant attachment style

00:01:16.919 --> 00:01:19.110
feels uncomfortable with intimacy.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.413
(soft violin music)

00:01:22.413 --> 00:01:23.949
When they get close to another person,

00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:25.618
they tend to panic and pull away.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.860
- Hey, I wanna tell you something.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:27.693
- M-hm?

00:01:27.693 --> 00:01:28.526
- I love you.

00:01:28.526 --> 00:01:30.361
- It's late, I have to go,

00:01:30.361 --> 00:01:31.617
and wash my friend's bird.

00:01:31.617 --> 00:01:33.210
- What are you talking about?

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.038
- Later, ha ha, see you around!

00:01:35.038 --> 00:01:36.796
- I just said I love you!

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:40.237
(soft violin music)

00:01:40.237 --> 00:01:42.172
- No, no, don't even, please don't.

00:01:42.172 --> 00:01:43.005
(whoosh)

00:01:43.005 --> 00:01:44.731
- According to a study done in the 1980s,

00:01:44.731 --> 00:01:47.133
56 percent of people are secure,

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:48.909
19 percent are anxious,

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:50.642
and 25 percent are avoidant.

00:01:50.642 --> 00:01:52.876
What can you do if you're
an anxious or an avoidant?

00:01:52.876 --> 00:01:54.418
One way you can improve your relationships

00:01:54.418 --> 00:01:55.869
is by learning more.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:01:56.796
Talk to a therapist,

00:01:56.796 --> 00:01:59.230
read books and articles
about attachment theory,

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.509
educate yourself,

00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:02.286
- Also, two insecure attachers

00:02:02.286 --> 00:02:04.292
do not work well with one another.

00:02:04.292 --> 00:02:05.840
- Hi, I'm a classic avoidant.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.527
- Hi, textbook anxious. Nice to meet you.

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:09.812
- Nice to meet you too.

00:02:09.812 --> 00:02:11.841
By the way, as soon as we fall in love,

00:02:11.841 --> 00:02:14.340
I will panic and immediately run away.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:15.697
- Oh, that's perfect
because as soon as you start

00:02:15.697 --> 00:02:17.518
to run away I'm gonna get super clingy,

00:02:17.518 --> 00:02:19.023
like do you have a Facebook, an Instagram,

00:02:19.023 --> 00:02:20.183
I'm gonna stalk everything.

00:02:20.183 --> 00:02:21.369
- You sound like a disaster.

00:02:21.369 --> 00:02:22.202
- I am.

00:02:22.202 --> 00:02:23.836
- I'm gonna disappear, it'll
be like I never existed.

00:02:23.836 --> 00:02:24.876
- Oh, that's gonna devastate me.

00:02:24.876 --> 00:02:25.745
- I'm so turned on right now.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:26.578
- Same.

00:02:26.578 --> 00:02:27.411
(whoosh)

00:02:27.411 --> 00:02:28.440
- If you're an anxious or an avoidant,

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:31.106
try being in a relationship
with a secure person.

00:02:31.106 --> 00:02:33.347
Being with a secure person
can calm your neuroses

00:02:33.347 --> 00:02:35.148
and put you at ease.

00:02:35.148 --> 00:02:36.130
- I'm gonna use the bathroom,

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:36.963
I'll be right back.

00:02:36.963 --> 00:02:38.212
- Oh you don't have to
tell me where you're going.

00:02:38.212 --> 00:02:39.681
Look, I am completely secure now, okay?

00:02:39.681 --> 00:02:40.907
So you can go to the bathroom,

00:02:40.907 --> 00:02:42.028
you can flirt with other women,

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:42.914
I mean, you could text your ex,

00:02:42.914 --> 00:02:44.480
I mean, we wanna have
an open relationship,

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.756
we could talk about that, I don't care.

00:02:45.756 --> 00:02:46.985
- I don't wanna do any of that.

00:02:46.985 --> 00:02:48.834
- Oh good, thank God, I
don't wanna that either.

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.449
- Whatever your attachment style is,

00:02:50.449 --> 00:02:51.997
you are worthy of love,

00:02:51.997 --> 00:02:54.695
and can still have
successful relationships.

00:02:54.695 --> 00:02:56.412
So just be aware of your patterns,

00:02:56.412 --> 00:02:58.239
and make positive choices.

00:02:58.239 --> 00:03:01.566
Also, I've been drinkin'
margaritas since 10 a.m.

00:03:01.566 --> 00:03:04.683
so I'm feelin' pretty positive.

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:07.264
(slurp)

00:03:07.264 --> 00:03:08.865
It's gonna be a good summer.

00:03:08.865 --> 00:03:09.852
(smack)

00:03:09.852 --> 00:03:11.546
I can feel it.

00:03:11.546 --> 00:03:14.129
(mellow music)

00:03:17.127 --> 00:03:18.345
(whooshing)

00:03:18.345 --> 00:03:19.479
(squeaking)

